ival reniro is basically  fighting a losing battle Alison and Otto  are clearly biased and vaman has a good  point in that he wants the blood of  valerians to stand the Throne of  driftmark up to this point we are  basically ruling out that visceros won't  be able to help rhaenyra so it was a  great twist for him to suddenly show up  here this may technically count as a  deus ex machina which in of itself I  find funny that this limping man is deus  ex machina to begin with but it was set  up that he expressed the interest in  having dinner so it's believable for him  to show up since he may have a burst of  energy there are two other aspects that  really sell this moment which is where  mean jawadi's Triumph and score and the  director dedicating an entire four  minutes of visares just limping to the  throne this long duration really sells  his struggles and without the music to  punctuate how big of a deal this is that  it wouldn't have been as Grand like  imagine the scene without the music and  it's just if it starts limping across  the throne room a flat out wouldn't work  so Ramin jawadi is great as always and  even has another moment to shine later  on in the episode but since we are in  the scene we may as well address the  elephant in the room which is vaymond  valerion it was so satisfying for him to  get mad and finally drop the bomb of  calling Rainier's children bastards it  kind of happened in the last episode but  it wasn't as explosive because aegon was  kind of awkwardly calling attention to  the fact that they look nothing like  valerians but here Damon is so  emotionally charged that it's immensely  satisfying when he yells that word and  it echoes throughout the throne room  oh bastards  the craters also gave Raymond quite a  bit of screen time before this scene to  build up this moment and even before  this episode it was always leading here  this is kind of like a mirror to vaman's  eulogy where he's expressing this notion  through his eyes but